  "solution": {
    "approach": "Print the first number followed immediately by the second number zero-padded to width 17.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1)",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1)",
    "code": {
      "C": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint main() {\n    long long a, b;\n    if (scanf(\"%lld %lld\", &a, &b) == 2) {\n        printf(\"%lld%017lld\\n\", a, b);\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "C++": "#include <iostream>\n#include <iomanip>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    long long a, b;\n    if (cin >> a >> b) {\n        cout << a << setfill('0') << setw(17) << b << \"\\n\";\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "Java": "import java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        if (sc.hasNextLong()) {\n            long a = sc.nextLong();\n            long b = sc.nextLong();\n            System.out.printf(\"%d%017d\\n\", a, b);\n        }\n    }\n}\n",
      "Python3": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    parts = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if len(parts) >= 2:\n        print(f\"{parts[0]}{int(parts[1]):017d}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n",
      "JavaScript": "const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction main() {\n    const parts = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf-8').trim().split(/\\s+/);\n    if (parts.length >= 2) {\n        console.log(parts[0] + parts[1].padStart(17, '0'));\n    }\n}\n\nmain();\n"
    },
    "notes": "Ensure edge case and standard I/O format handling.",
    "editorial": "Format the first integer and format the second integer padded with leading zeros to 17 characters."
  },
  "hints": [
    "In C, printf(\"%lld%017lld\", a, b) formats b with 17 digits with leading zeros.",
    "In Python, f'{a}{b:017d}'.",
    "In JavaScript, string b is padded with b.padStart(17, '0')."
  ],
